  "sequestered_use": "\u00a76.2: a future uncontaminated rerun only. The eighth was never materialised in this repository, so enlarging the composed set from it means authoring topics, which is a governed bank change",
  "why_k_is_6": "\u00a713.14's verdict is a conjunction over entries, so a margin meant to make a probe pass IMPLY a Gate-4 pass is family-wise over the entries it covers. Six is the base arm's entry count: solo:A, solo:B and both orders of A with B, which are the only Gate-4 entries whose instruments both exist when the probe runs",
  "why_that_ceiling": "a margin wider than 0.95 - FOCAL_AIM refuses, on its solo B cell alone and before any composition, an operating point sitting exactly where \u00a712.3 aims. A probe that refuses the registered aim is not a feasibility check"
 },
